  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.Vivekanandan vs The Food Safety Officer on 18 March, 2024 Author: M.Dhandapani Bench: M.Dhandapani Crl.O.P.(MD)No.14628 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 18.03.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Dhandapani Crl.O.P.(MD) No.14628 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.(MD).Nos.9489 and 9492 of 2022 P.Vivekanandan ... Petitioner Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Code No.109 and 120, Chellampatti & Vadipatti Taluk, Designated Officers Office, Multipurpose Health Supervisors (F) Training School, Viswanathapuram, Madurai-625 014. ... Respondent Prayer:",
    "facts": "ORDER This petition has been filed to quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No.10 of 2022 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate, Vadipatti. 2. The petitioner is the first accused. This petition has been filed mainly on the ground that the charge sheet filed against the manufatureres/Accused Nos. 2 and 3 was [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court in Crl.O.P(MD).No.12283 of 2022 dated 29.08.2022. 3. A2 and A3 are doing the business of groundnut oil and A3 is the owner of the A2's company. After manufacuturing the groundnut oil, they sent the same for sale through the petitioner. While so, on 25.08.2020, the respondent/food safety officer visited the petitioners factory and taken the sample and sent the same for analysis and the report was received on 19.10.2020. Thereafter, the present complaint was registered on the ground that the edigible oil, which was taken by the food safety officer is unsafe. However, the edigible oil was packed by the manufacuter on 06.03.2020 and it is usable on or before six months (i.e) on 05.09.2020. In such circumstances, the food analyst analyzed the groundnut oil from https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.14628 of 2022 02.09.2020 to 29.09.2020, which is beyond the period of usable date (i.e) on 05.09.2020. The analysis was done after the expiry period date, on that sole ground, the prosecution initiated against the co-accused namely A2 and A3 was [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court. 4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor appearing for the respondent submitted that the food sample was anaylized after the expiry period, on that sole ground, this Court [LEAKAGE_MASK] the complaint in respect of the A2 and A3. Under these circumstances, after the best usable period, the sample was subjected for analysis. The referral lab opportunity notice was sent to the petitioner on 29.10.2020.",
    "arguments": "The learned conunsel for the petitioner submitted that the petitioner is the retailer and he was arrayed as A1 in the compliant. 6.The learned Counsel appearing for the petitioner during the course of the argument submitted that the period mentioned in the label 'best before' is a mandatory one and he was prevented from selling the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.14628 of 2022 food.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned conunsel for the petitioner submitted that the petitioner is the retailer and he was arrayed as A1 in the compliant. 6.The learned Counsel appearing for the petitioner during the course of the argument submitted that the period mentioned in the label 'best before' is a mandatory one and he was prevented from selling the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.14628 of 2022 food.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
